{"title":"1962 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find the smallest natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> which has the following properties:\n</p><p>(a) Its decimal representation has 6 as the last digit.\n</p><p>(b) If the last digit 6 is erased and placed in front of the remaining digits, the resulting number is four times as large as the original number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> which satisfy the inequality:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ced9beddeacb856f71f58a3de06d4bb433e67065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\sqrt{3-x}-\\sqrt{x+1}}&gt;\\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"189\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the cube <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/621a50d522ad9e2e8b3678ee3c5c2e4e06476683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDA&#39;B&#39;C&#39;D&#39;$\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4aa4d85335863f762ae4128b05ede6d4e918678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;D&#39;$\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> are the upper and lower bases, respectively, and edges <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59f5d75cc27d504ede022aab803742e799709f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA&#39;$\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae0e30605dc87c83aecb3f588afa7129bee6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b7058f8a28ca225136b284b337138a54e39e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/825000b887cf170e8a54ee5dcdafffbdfb959cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DD&#39;$\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> are parallel). The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> moves at constant speed along the perimeter of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> in the direction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba5021fe27d82e2a3e3c293e409b60edaee4d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDA$\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, and the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> moves at the same rate along the perimeter of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8701771ab21f00a17b02edf89b1ada183f2bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39;CB$\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> in the direction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bf5c921abfaa19716cc897200cc255ca714771b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39;CBB&#39;$\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> begin their motion at the same instant from the starting positions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Determine and draw the locus of the midpoints of the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Solve the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a72f688ddfbd7345dff7bf5178effe035c1935c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cos^2{x}+cos^2{2x}+cos^2{3x}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>On the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> there are given three distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9874ea56cf8fec1bd246793224fbcfaad17ab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Construct (using only straightedge and compass) a fourth point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> such that a circle can be inscribed in the quadrilateral thus obtained.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider an isosceles triangle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of its circumscribed circle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/0027034d8a10372a06deaf4f4084c01956587479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rho$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"9\" height=\"11\" /> the radius of its inscribed circle. Prove that the distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between the centers of these two circles is \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/051a64f293508aad41b5262146f6db9cb1553d06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\sqrt{r(r-2p)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"124\" height=\"32\" />.</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc58cda5e5eb229937fae0f8bed1d0364ae8169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SABC$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> has the following property: there exist five spheres, each tangent to the edges <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/0663b872aab5d82c5a03a0427838923ebee49b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SA, SB, SC, BC, CA, AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"202\" height=\"16\" />, or to their extensions.\n</p><p>(a) Prove that the tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc58cda5e5eb229937fae0f8bed1d0364ae8169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SABC$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> is regular.\n</p><p>(b) Prove conversely that for every regular tetrahedron five such spheres exist.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 7\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO\" title=\"1962 IMO\">1962 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1962\">IMO 1962 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO\" title=\"1962 IMO\">1962 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO\" title=\"1961 IMO\">1961 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_IMO\" title=\"1963 IMO\">1963 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018041417\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 227/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 836/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5745/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.452      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.452      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5852:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018041417 and revision id 132269. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}